From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: match restored init status

The status-gated physical image reaches the post-RESTORE_SOME status marker,
but the retained value is 0x8002 after RESTORE_SOME has rewritten CP0_STATUS,
not the pre-restore 0x8004 recorded by the C return path.

Match the status value observed at the assembly decision point. Other kernel
returns in the same trace use 0x8003 after the same mask, so this keeps the
direct stub branch limited to the final /init return.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/entry.S | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@ restore_partial:		# restore partial frame
 	sw	k1, 20(k0)
 	lw	k1, 24(k0)
 	sync
-	li	k0, 0x8004
+	li	k0, 0x8002
 	bne	k1, k0, 1f
 	 nop
 	mfc0	k1, CP0_EBASE
-- 
2.45.0
